\title{scimagR: Spinal Cord Injury Imaging Pipeline for MRI and CT Analysis}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.svg}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

An end-to-end pipeline for longitudinal magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) and computed tomography (CT) analysis in spinal cord injury (SCI) research. Provides R wrappers for the 'Spinal Cord Toolbox' (SCT; De Leener et al. (2017) \doi{10.1016/j.neuroimage.2016.10.009}), including 'SCIsegV2' lesion segmentation, DICOM anonymization and NIfTI conversion helpers built on 'pydicom' and 'dcm2niix', SCI-specific clinical metrics (maximum spinal cord compression, compression ratio, tissue bridge quantification), implant artifact grading, and pipeline orchestration with built-in quality control. Integrates with 'workflowr' for reproducible, publication-ready neuroimaging analyses. All external tools are optional; the metrics, registry, quality-control and plotting functions work without them.
